The Grib-Index-Kerchunk method extends the dynamic GRIB chunking approach
originally prototyped in nextgen-dmac
(https://github.com/asascience-open/nextgen-dmac, commit 6b3286627070).

Portions of gfs/dynamic_zarr_store.py and gfs/test_dynamic_zarr_store.py
are derived from upstream code copyright 2023 Camus Energy, licensed
under the MIT License. The original copyright notice is preserved in
the source headers of those files.

This product depends on, but does not redistribute, the following
upstream open-source libraries: kerchunk (MIT), fsspec (BSD-3),
xarray (Apache-2.0), gribberish (MIT), Herbie (MIT), Lithops (Apache-2.0).
